  "scope": "comprehensive-overflow-v1",
  "notes": [
    "Arabic source Arabic Judith follows Jerome's Vulgate (Latin) recension; English English follows Rahlfs Greek Septuagint. Vulgate Judith is famously a free retelling — Jerome translated it from a now-lost Aramaic source, and the result diverges substantially from the Greek both in content selection and ordering.",
    "Unlike TOB (where ar consistently has more verses), JDT has BIDIRECTIONAL overflow:",
    "  - en > ar in chapters 1, 2, 7, 8, 10, 11, 14: LXX gives detailed military / scene-setting narrative that Vulgate condenses.",
    "  - ar > en in chapters 3, 4, 5, 9, 13, 15, 16: Vulgate adds extended speeches, prayers, and post-victory ceremony.",
    "Mappings cover the overflow region (verses past the other translation's chapter max) and the well-attested mid-chapter shifts in ch9 (Judith's prayer) and the Holofernes-encounter chapters."
  ],
